libretv provides LibreTV 2.24.0 from the official release standalone bundle,
installed under tools/libretv/.

Launcher
  Linux/macOS: tools/libretv/libretv
  Windows:     tools/libretv\libretv.cmd

Run
  PASSWORD=your-password libretv
  PASSWORD=your-password PORT=8080 libretv   # PORT defaults to 3000

PASSWORD is required; the site prompts for administrator setup if it is not
set. Other optional environment variables (PROXY_SECRET, DEFAULT_SOURCES,
DEFAULT_LIVE_SOURCES, etc.) are passed through unchanged.

Runtime requirement
  Node.js 18+ is required. The launcher prefers Node from PATH and falls back
  to the nodejs22 host tool when the 'nodejs22' feature is enabled. If neither
  is usable it prints an error and exits with code 127.

Conditional nodejs22 dependency
  The manifest declares a 'nodejs22' feature whose dependency is the standalone
  host tool port nodejs22. Use the provided install.sh / install.ps1 script: it
  checks the system Node first and enables the feature only when no usable
  Node is present, so vcpkg installs nodejs22 exactly in that case.
  Example: ./install.sh --vcpkg-root /path/to/vcpkg --triplet x64-linux
  The dependency is visible with:
    vcpkg depend-info 'libretv[nodejs22]' --overlay-ports=... --format=tree

The release bundle is architecture independent and ships its runtime
node_modules, so no npm install or native build is performed at packaging time.
